I think so, too.

258
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:36,880
Keep your wits about you, Sanji.

259
00:17:37,060 --> 00:17:37,937
This isn't a game.

260
00:17:38,020 --> 00:17:43,220
If you lose focus now,
she's gonna kill you!

261
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:47,797
Merit!

262
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:49,660
Merit! Merit!

263
00:17:50,020 --> 00:17:50,940
Merit!

264
00:17:53,440 --> 00:18:00,200
I had a taste of love and sorrow too.

265
00:18:01,280 --> 00:18:07,197
I found love and I was
hurt, but I never lost hope.

266
00:18:07,280 --> 00:18:09,317
And now I'll leave the gold.

267
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:11,377
Count the iron.

268
00:18:11,460 --> 00:18:13,477
Even if.

269
00:18:13,560 --> 00:18:15,477
Rain pours down.

270
00:18:15,560 --> 00:18:17,457
Even if.

271
00:18:17,540 --> 00:18:19,057
Danger comes.

272
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:22,317
Stay close, never let go.

273
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:24,337
And let your passion grow.

274
00:18:24,420 --> 00:18:30,780
A symbol of your mom.

275
00:18:34,040 --> 00:18:36,640
When in the day.

276
00:19:00,780 --> 00:19:02,000
Thank you.

277
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:43,460
It's good for a king.

278
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:44,740
No, a kingdom.

279
00:19:45,380 --> 00:19:46,210
Yummy.

280
00:19:46,880 --> 00:19:49,700
This cake is worthy of
a double-pate strength.

281
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:51,940
Splendid work, Struzan.

282
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:54,475
Why, I simply can't praise you enough.

283
00:19:54,700 --> 00:19:56,260
Just doing my duty, Mama.

284
00:19:56,780 --> 00:19:59,720
I can't wait to try it.

285
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,360
Oh, look, this lovely cake.

286
00:20:12,580 --> 00:20:14,180
It's going to be our altar.

287
00:20:15,780 --> 00:20:17,580
You're lovely, my dear.

288
00:20:17,980 --> 00:20:19,000
No, stop.

289
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:21,220
Gosh, you are so silly.

290
00:20:22,140 --> 00:20:23,220
And so did.

291
00:20:23,940 --> 00:20:25,880
Oh, Pudding, so cute.

292
00:20:26,060 --> 00:20:28,537
She looks just like me
when I was that age.

293
00:20:28,620 --> 00:20:30,300
And how long ago was that?

294
00:20:30,780 --> 00:20:32,840
Well, someone has a death wish.

295
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:34,390
No!

296
00:20:36,080 --> 00:20:38,200
My, my, my, my.

297
00:20:39,580 --> 00:20:41,480
Enjoy it while it lasts,

298
00:20:41,700 --> 00:20:46,660
my hapless little friends, because
soon it will all come crashing down.

299
00:20:59,940 --> 00:21:02,340
We're nearly at the climax.

300
00:21:03,100 --> 00:21:06,580
Here, please enjoy the
wedding from these VIP seats.

301
00:21:09,220 --> 00:21:12,400
Yes, you'll want a
front row view for this.

302
00:21:12,700 --> 00:21:14,400
Your own execution.

303
00:21:15,260 --> 00:21:17,920
Let the moon and the bride and groom kiss.

304
00:21:18,300 --> 00:21:20,500
Our bloody banquet will begin.

305
00:21:21,300 --> 00:21:24,320
Sorry, Vince, folks, but you gotta go.

306
00:21:24,980 --> 00:21:25,810
Finally.

307
00:21:29,300 --> 00:21:31,960
Old Sanji really lucked out, didn't he?

308
00:21:32,240 --> 00:21:35,957
If I'd have known pudding was that
hot, I would have married her myself.

309
00:21:36,040 --> 00:21:37,511
Marry Big Mom's daughter?

310
00:21:37,720 --> 00:21:38,600
No thanks.

311
00:21:38,840 --> 00:21:40,657
Sanji's nothing but a sacrifice.

312
00:21:40,740 --> 00:21:41,660
Remember that.

313
00:21:42,260 --> 00:21:46,157
Once he's married, he'll be under Big
Mom's thumb for the rest of his life.

314
00:21:46,240 --> 00:21:47,070
Hard pass.

315
00:21:47,300 --> 00:21:49,124
That's the last thing I'd want.

316
00:21:49,980 --> 00:21:50,900
I see.

317
00:21:51,220 --> 00:21:54,338
We're surrounded by the
strongest Charlotte siblings.

318
00:21:55,300 --> 00:21:57,340
Rather easy targets, aren't we?

319
00:21:58,560 --> 00:22:00,860
And sitting ducks since we're unarmed.

320
00:22:03,220 --> 00:22:04,220
That's fine.

321
00:22:04,580 --> 00:22:07,100
The world is better off without Germa.

322
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:11,100
Well, most of us at least.

323
00:22:16,400 --> 00:22:18,557
You have to escape Sanji.

324
00:22:18,640 --> 00:22:20,297
You have a plan, right?

325
00:22:20,380 --> 00:22:22,797
But can I trust Captain Luffy?

326
00:22:22,880 --> 00:22:29,077
I want to do you, Sanji—take pudding
to be your lawfully wedded wife,

327
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:32,157
to have and to hold in
sickness and in health,

328
00:22:32,240 --> 00:22:35,617
for richer or for poorer,
till death do you part!

329
00:22:35,700 --> 00:22:36,530
part

330
00:22:37,600 --> 00:22:39,320
Hey guys, hurry!

331
00:22:39,680 --> 00:22:41,060
We're gonna be late!

332
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:42,440
That's your fault!

333
00:22:42,660 --> 00:22:43,980
Don't complain to us!

334
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:49,060
Do you plan to remain loyal and
to love and cherish each other?

335
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:57,340
I can hardly believe
it's all coming together.

336
00:23:10,700 --> 00:23:12,040
What's wrong, Pudding?

337
00:23:12,440 --> 00:23:13,793
Why are you collapsing?

338
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:18,880
Now, you may lift the
veil and kiss the bride.

339
00:23:19,260 --> 00:23:20,640
Katakuri, what's wrong?

340
00:23:21,760 --> 00:23:24,020
You saw the future, didn't you?

341
00:23:30,160 --> 00:23:32,340
This is it. You ready?

342
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:34,830
Yes.

343
00:23:38,540 --> 00:23:40,920
Thank you.

344
00:24:15,700 --> 00:24:17,600
Take a good look, Sanji.

345
00:24:18,520 --> 00:24:23,017
Let's see how you feel
when you see my hideous.

346
00:24:23,100 --> 00:24:25,140
third eye.

347
00:24:36,320 --> 00:24:37,760
Good boy.

348
00:24:38,220 --> 00:24:40,260
Stay just like that.

349
00:24:43,660 --> 00:24:47,160
To think that you were
hiding such a beautiful eye.

350
00:25:17,640 --> 00:25:20,760
Sorry, I, uh, no, I shouldn't stare.

351
00:25:21,040 --> 00:25:22,820
It's just so pretty.

352
00:25:24,020 --> 00:25:25,220
What's she doing?

353
00:25:25,760 --> 00:25:26,940
Shoot him, Pudding.

354
00:25:28,140 --> 00:25:30,040
Are you okay?

355
00:25:31,980 --> 00:25:33,240
You idiot.

356
00:25:33,640 --> 00:25:34,816
What are you saying?

357
00:25:36,080 --> 00:25:40,900
Then, when the happy couple appears,
we'll see Sanji, the man of the hour.

358
00:25:41,820 --> 00:25:46,702
Suddenly, much to his shock and horror, he
will discover that you have a third eye.

359
00:25:47,020 --> 00:25:49,180
He expected a beautiful face,

360
00:25:49,320 --> 00:25:53,260
but now he sees his bride for
the monster that she truly is.

361
00:25:53,880 --> 00:25:55,960
He'll be paralyzed with shock.

362
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:09,500
Screw you.

363
00:26:10,200 --> 00:26:11,860
Why are you doing this?

364
00:26:13,960 --> 00:26:16,660
I've never heard those
words once in my life.

365
00:26:17,140 --> 00:26:19,258
You're just lying to me, aren't you?

366
00:26:19,540 --> 00:26:22,246
No one would ever think
this eye is beautiful.

367
00:26:22,780 --> 00:26:24,721
There's something wrong with you.

368
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:26,640
What is going on, Pudding?

369
00:26:26,880 --> 00:26:27,880
Kill him already.

370
00:26:29,820 --> 00:26:31,220
No one has ever.

371
00:26:36,080 --> 00:26:38,857
You're my daughter, but that
eye still creeps me out.

372
00:26:38,940 --> 00:26:41,058
Cover it with your bangs, would you?

373
00:26:43,660 --> 00:26:45,740
Yes, ma 'am. I will.

374
00:26:48,020 --> 00:26:49,360
What's that eye?

375
00:26:50,420 --> 00:26:53,900
It's really creeping
me out, little monster.

376
00:26:56,640 --> 00:26:58,680
It's Rose, you're a weirdo!

377
00:26:58,920 --> 00:26:59,780
Please stop!

378
00:27:00,720 --> 00:27:02,080
Leave me alone!

379
00:27:08,780 --> 00:27:10,820
There, that's much better.

380
00:27:10,920 --> 00:27:12,840
Little freak, little freak.

381
00:27:17,340 --> 00:27:18,360
That's it.

382
00:27:18,600 --> 00:27:20,540
I've had enough.

383
00:27:21,380 --> 00:27:23,080
Bastards, bastards.

384
00:27:23,720 --> 00:27:27,000
I'll murder all of you. Get away.

385
00:27:38,740 --> 00:27:39,570
Pudding?

386
00:27:41,360 --> 00:27:42,860
You go to hell!

387
00:27:43,720 --> 00:27:46,000
Is this pity? Dammit!

388
00:27:47,120 --> 00:27:48,457
Pastor, it's beautiful!

389
00:27:48,540 --> 00:27:50,320
How dare you tell me that!

390
00:27:51,800 --> 00:27:54,080
Are you gonna do this or not, Pudding?

391
00:27:55,500 --> 00:27:57,460
What's wrong? Talk to me.

392
00:28:00,040 --> 00:28:01,820
Priest, he'll do it!

393
00:28:07,360 --> 00:28:09,200
That's no use. He'll miss.

394
00:28:23,840 --> 00:28:25,080
He dodged.

395
00:28:29,260 --> 00:28:31,400
Don't let me down, Straw Hat.

396
00:28:31,660 --> 00:28:35,340
Luffy, that's your cue. Go! Right! Ready!

397
00:28:38,320 --> 00:28:39,737
Was that a gunshot?

398
00:28:39,820 --> 00:28:42,717
The priest did it—no, he got shot. Why?

399
00:28:42,800 --> 00:28:45,257
What is going on here?

400
00:28:45,340 --> 00:28:46,480
Could it be why

401
00:28:48,180 --> 00:28:50,137
the hell didn't pudding shoot him?

402
00:28:50,220 --> 00:28:52,437
Katakuri, tell me what you see.

403
00:28:52,520 --> 00:28:55,557
We have a bigger problem,
mama—something completely unexpected.

404
00:28:55,640 --> 00:28:59,737
Even I can't stop this. What now?

405
00:28:59,820 --> 00:29:01,997
We fight or are we waiting?

406
00:29:02,080 --> 00:29:04,840
we waiting So is this something new?

407
00:29:05,580 --> 00:29:06,940
Almost there!

408
00:29:07,720 --> 00:29:09,520
Please forgive me, Mama.

409
00:29:10,200 --> 00:29:12,660
I had no choice but to do what they said.

410
00:29:13,100 --> 00:29:15,180
It's time to take Sanji back!

411
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:21,240
What now?

412
00:29:21,620 --> 00:29:23,220
I can't stop them.

413
00:29:24,380 --> 00:29:26,556
They're going to pop out of the cake.

414
00:29:27,140 --> 00:29:27,970
What?

415
00:29:46,540 --> 00:29:48,340
Let's go!

416
00:30:02,740 --> 00:30:04,620
I didn't know!

417
00:30:10,160 --> 00:30:10,990
Oh my God!

418
00:30:12,740 --> 00:30:13,570
Oh my God!

419
00:30:13,653 --> 00:30:18,100
Oh my God!
